From 6d4de5859bcaa6a5f3b5537f9043c92b9c2b2571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:33:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hal: a held frame's engine-A composite memoised (the pause
 menu composed once)

A pause screen puts a layer behind the 3D over all 49152 cells, so every
pass of the composite runs over the whole screen: 33-35 ms of a 3DS tick,
while the menu waits for input and the picture holds still. With
port_message_composite_memo(1), a frame held on the card whose inputs are
byte for byte the last recorded frame's replays that frame's result: the
spans its blit wrote, the brightness mask, and the facts later code reads
(the mask's flags, kept/buried, a cell behind the 3D, the signature).

The inputs are compared, not hashed: the host answers the raster asks for
(each sprite's routed shift and seam-snow answer, the gapless shift, the
arrows' reanchor, the HUD layout, the picture's size, the per-line windows)
and the memory it reads (DISPCNT and the BG, window and blend registers,
the 3D clear colour, both palettes, OAM, each enabled BG's map and tiles,
the OBJ tiles each shown sprite can reach). A frame is recorded only when
plain (held, spans only, no arrow capture, no lift, no 2D on the card, no
probe armed, the HUD row's star-counter edge at rest), and the memo is
tried only after a frame that blitted 8192 cells or more
(SM64DS_COMPA_MEMO_CELLS). SM64DS_COMPA_MEMO_VERIFY=1 composes every frame
and counts results that differ from the replay's; the [compa] line carries
the counts and a memo zone.
